{"question": "How many loads were delivered in the last full month available in the data?", "generated_sql": "WITH max_date AS (\n  SELECT max(date_day) AS max_d FROM main_analytics.dim_date\n),\nlast_full_month AS (\n  SELECT CASE\n           WHEN max_d = last_day(max_d) THEN date_trunc('month', max_d)\n           ELSE date_trunc('month', max_d) - INTERVAL '1 month'\n         END AS month_start\n  FROM max_date\n)\nSELECT count(*) AS delivered_loads_last_full_month\nFROM main_analytics.fct_loads f\nJOIN last_full_month lfm\n  ON date_trunc('month', f.delivery_date) = lfm.month_start\nWHERE f.is_delivered = true", "answer": [{"delivered_loads_last_full_month": 0}], "id": "q1", "assumption": "Interpret \"last full month available\" as the latest complete calendar month before the final partial delivery month. In this dataset, March 2025 has one delivery dated March 15, so February 2025 is treated as the last full month, even though it has no delivered rows."}
{"question": "Which shipper had the highest total book price?", "generated_sql": "SELECT s.shipper_name, SUM(f.book_price) AS total_book_price\nFROM main_analytics.fct_loads f\nJOIN main_analytics.dim_shipper s ON f.shipper_key = s.shipper_key\nGROUP BY s.shipper_name\nORDER BY total_book_price DESC\nLIMIT 1", "answer": [{"shipper_name": "Shipper 1249", "total_book_price": 1915694.1600000001}], "id": "q2", "assumption": "Use all modeled loads, not only delivered loads, because the question does not specify delivered."}
